Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — the markup with `@typeparam TItem`, rendering each item via `ItemTemplate` with Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — the `partial class` code-behind:
- Copies `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the passed-in list).
- Swaps elements on button click, then invokes `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only copy of the reordered list.

Usage matches your example — just note the callback signature is `EventCallback<IReadOnlyList<TItem>>`:

```csharp
private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
{
    tasks = newOrder.ToList();
}
```
